  "id": "COMPOUND:27169 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Manzamine A is shown to have a target of DNA polymerase iota, which is in turn targeted by (3R,3S)-3-O-Methylviolanone and Debilisone D. These compounds are all linked to FaDu, suggesting a potential pathway where Manzamine A may exert its effects through the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Manzamine A and FaDu, with the target of DNA polymerase iota being a critical node in this relationship. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same enzyme, along with their shared target FaDu, indicates a possible mode of action involving DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways suggests that Manzamine A may act through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota, potentially leading to cellular dysfunction in FaDu. The evidence is consistent with a biologically plausible mechanism, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact role of Manzamine A in this context.",
